WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.767
-Jenna Ortega.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.067
Welcome to the show.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.234
-Thank you very much,
Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.901
-Thanks for being here.
I appreciate this.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.634
It's good to have --
Before we go into "Wednesday,"

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:10.534
which I can't wait
to rave about,

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.634
right now, you're in a trailer
for the new "Scream" movie.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.834
-Yes, I am.
-And it broke records --

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.367
it started --
it went viral, I think.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:19.567
It came out and it did 3 million
views in the first day.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.767
This is your second
"Scream" movie.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.100
Do you like doing these movies?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.901
-I love horror films.
I don't know what it is about,

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.467
you know, having blood
thrown on your face

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.968
and running around
screaming bloody murder,

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.801
but it really is so therapeutic,
so much fun.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.234
Everyone who works
on horror sets loves horror.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.934
You know,
people do special effects

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.167
because they grew up
loving gore.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.701
The best part about
the "Scream" films is,

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.701
it really is
such a great community.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.968
That cast and crew,
they're my family.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.400
And we can never
take anything seriously.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.968
So, Ghostface could literally
be in the middle

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.801
of their monologue,
and we're having

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.734
to restart takes because
we're laughing so hard.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.234
-Oh, really?
-Yeah. It's a mess.

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.901
-On one of the scariest movies
ever, you're laughing?

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.601
-Yeah, we could be --
In the fifth one, I was, like,

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:03.133
army crawling in the hospital,
and I just would --

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:06.033
I wouldn't lift my face 'cause
I was laughing in my hands.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.434
-Do you feel like you're
being kind of typecast

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.767
because you're in that,
and you're in "Wednesday."

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.834
They're kind of dark.
-It's something about my face.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:14.834
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:15.934
-Yeah.
I don't know what it is.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.567
People love seeing me scared.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.033
-No.
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.667
-You are --
Not only are you stunning,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.167
but you can't take your eyes
off of you when I see you.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.934
I watch "Wednesday,"
and I told you this backstage.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.968
I go, "Oh, my gosh.
You're crushing this."

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.701
You're phenomenal.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:32.334
It is the second-most watched
series in Netflix history.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:33.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:39.067
One of only three shows to be
streamed over a billion times.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:41.033
Over a billion.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.734
Can you even understand that?
-No.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.334
I try not to, actually.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.667
-It's too weird.
-But, I mean, you nail

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.501
every joke, every delivery.
You're so funny.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:51.100
This is before
you even did the dance scene.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.767
I mean, the dan--
Can we talk about the dance?

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.968
The Wednesday dance?
-Yeah, if you want to.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.801
-Yeah, I mean, going into it,
what happened?

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.634
Did Tim Burton go,
"Okay, I got an idea.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:01.834
You do this, you do that."

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.901
-Well, I read episode 104
pretty early on.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.868
And we didn't know what song
we were gonna be using,

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.167
we didn't know what
the situation was.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.400
Initially,
they wanted a flash mob,

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.868
but I thought, no,
there's no way Wednesday

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.767
would be cool with dancing and
encouraging a bunch of people.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.934
So Tim and I -- the director,
Tim Burton, and I

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.601
talked about it a little bit,
and he said,

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.133
"Yeah, let's not do a circle.
Let's have it be her own thing."

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:24.934
And I remember, about a week
before we started --

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:28.667
a week before we shot the dance,
he chose the song,

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.167
"Goo Goo Muck," by The Cramps.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.767
And The Cramps is one of my
favorite bands ever.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.300
So I was super excited,
super pumped.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.868
It was on my episode 4 playlist.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.701
And he came to my trailer
about two days before we shot it

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.934
and said, "Hey, Jenna, so I know
you said that you wanted to

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.501
choreograph this yourself --"

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.000
Because I refused
to see a choreographer.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.100
He was like,
"I know you've got it.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.300
You've been working on it.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.667
I'm not even worried about it.
I trust you."

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.167
And I said, "Oh, yeah,
you know, it's all so good."

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.968
And I had not gone over it
at all.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.767
-You had no plan?
-No.

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.367
I mean, I was doing cello
that week, fencing that week.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.534
I just didn't have time.
-You do a lot in the show.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.200
-There's a lot going on.
-Yes.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.200
You work hard on this show,
and, like, on top of that,

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.234
you're, like, gonna choreograph
your own dance?

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.601
-Yeah. Oh, my God.
I was kicking myself.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.400
I felt like such a fool.
I was like --

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.534
I'm not a dancer.
I don't do any of that.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.701
I have no experience
in that field.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.400
And then, yeah,
I didn't sleep for two days.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.434
I watched videos of
Siouxsie and the Banshees.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.868
-Really?
-Denis Lavant in "Beau Travail."

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.767
I found archival footage
of goth kids

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.634
dancing in clubs in the '80s.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.734
-Lene Lovich, Nina Hagen,

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.767
just anything that I could
get my hands on.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.734
And then, on the day, I thought,
"Well, all right."

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.601
-"I'm just gonna do it."
-"Let's just see what happens."

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.167
-Did you just go super long?

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.100
Did you do it
like a 20-minute dance?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.667
Or is this the step by step,

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.434
this was exactly
what you planned?

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.901
-No, I knew there were certain
things that I wanted to do.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.334
I paid homage to Lisa Loring,
the first Wednesday Addams.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.033
I did a little bit of her
shuffle that she does.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.400
And, of course,
they cut out of camera

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.634
when I did do it,
but it's there, I know it is.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.601
[ Laughs ]
-'Cause you did it, yeah.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.567
-Yeah.
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:01.801
That's wild.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.601
Did you understand
that it would go this viral?

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.501
It's everything
on TikTok right now.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:09.100
Right now, if you go on TikTok,
it's you dancing.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.834
It is.
-No, I didn't, I didn't.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.267
And Netflix,
they were telling me,

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.834
"Oh, you know, Jenna, this is
gonna be a thing on TikTok."

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.367
And I thought, "Yeah, yeah,
yeah, okay, whatever."

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.200
Because I figured, you know,
"They're excited.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.767
They're getting hyped up,"
and then they were right.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.534
-Yeah, sometimes
people are right.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.601
-Yeah, they know what they're
doing over there or something.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.534
-You're mesmerizing.
You're dazzling to look at.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.334
I just go, "Oh, my God."
And you're doing that,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.501
and you're just doing
the Wednesday stare,

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.534
and you're kind of doing that.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:31.934
But then that,
and it's kind of --

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.400
You make it cool.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.567
And it's one of the kind of
geekiest songs, "Goo Goo Muck."

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:37.934
♪ Wah wah wah ♪

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.434
You know, The Cramps, and I go,
"How did you do this?"

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:41.968
And it's just -- I don't know.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.767
I think we all agree
it's just well done.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:44.801
You just crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:50.601
-Jenna Ortega.
I want to show a clip.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.534
Here's Jenna Ortega in
"Wednesday."

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:53.934
Take a look at this.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:55.634
-Winner draws first blood.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:59.267
[ Suspenseful music ]

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:01.100
-[ Scoffs ]

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.334
-It's your decision, Bianca.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:07.400
♪♪

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.901
-Let's see if you bleed
in black and white.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:19.901
♪♪

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:29.901
♪♪

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:33.501
♪♪

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.434
[ Blade slices ]

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.701
♪♪

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:39.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:41.801
-Jenna Ortega!

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:43.968
"Wednesday" is streaming
right now on Netflix.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.434
We'll be right back
with stand-up

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:47.801
from Mike Feeney, everybody.
Come on back.

